{"slug":"bill-huizenga","qid":"Q862199","name":"Bill Huizenga","desc":"American politician","article":"Bill Huizenga","born":"1969-01-31","died":null,"birthplace":"Zeeland","parties":["Republican Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"MI-04","f":2023,"u":null},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"MI-02","f":2011,"u":2023},{"t":"Michigan House of Representatives","w":"","f":2003,"u":2009}],"summary":"William Patrick Huizenga ( HY-zing-gə; born January 31, 1969) is an American politician serving as a U.S. representative from Michigan since 2011, representing the state's 4th congressional district since 2023. A member of the Republican Party, Huizenga served in the Michigan House of Representatives from 2003 to 2009. His district covers much of Southwestern Michigan, including Kalamazoo, Battle Creek, and Holland.","photo":{"f":"bill-huizenga.jpg","by":"U.S. House of Representatives","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rep._Bill_Huizenga_-_118th_Congress_(portrait_crop).jpg"},"history":[{"y":2026,"o":"H","k":"MI-04","p":"R","n":"Bill Huizenga","race":"MI-04"},{"y":2024,"o":"H","k":"MI-04","p":"R","v":234489,"s":55.07,"w":true,"n":"Bill Huizenga"},{"y":2022,"o":"H","k":"MI-04","p":"R","v":183936,"s":54.36,"w":true,"n":"Bill Huizenga"},{"y":2020,"o":"H","k":"MI-02","p":"R","v":238711,"s":59.2,"w":true,"n":"Bill Huizenga"},{"y":2018,"o":"H","k":"MI-02","p":"R","v":168970,"s":55.32,"w":true,"n":"Bill Huizenga"},{"y":2016,"o":"H","k":"MI-02","p":"R","v":212508,"s":62.63,"w":true,"n":"Bill Huizenga"},{"y":2014,"o":"H","k":"MI-02","p":"R","v":135568,"s":63.63,"w":true,"n":"Bill Huizenga"},{"y":2012,"o":"H","k":"MI-02","p":"R","v":194653,"s":61.16,"w":true,"n":"Bill Huizenga"},{"y":2010,"o":"H","k":"MI-02","p":"R","v":148864,"s":65.27,"w":true,"n":"Bill Huizenga"}]}